<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mongols</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mongols are a nomadic people of the Mongolian steppe who were united under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a> in 1206. Their conquests created the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a> and reshaped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eurasia">Eurasia</a>, destroying states such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazmian-empire">Khwarazmian Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty</a> and threatening the Ayyubid and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> realms. Mongol rulers founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mongols.jpg" alt="Mongols" width="320" height="196" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sayf al-Vâhidî. Hérât. Afghanistan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bataille_entre_mongols_%26_chinois_(1211).jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
